s": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 429870, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01C6y7tFy4u4XEJ1b5HoCm1N", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 436956, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **The bug:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` said it used banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) but actually used ROUND_HALF_UP. So `2.665` came out as `2.67` instead of the expected `2.66`.\n- **The fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-bankers-rounding`, I changed the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` on commit `08d3cd5986` passed.\n- **The PR:** The request to open it timed out, so I checked the open PRs before retrying. The PR had been created, but with no reviewers, so I added alex separately rather than opening a duplicate.\n\nI couldn't confirm the FIN-212 requirement itself because the advisory lookup returned \"unknown advisory.\" I went by the docstring and the test. I haven't merged the PR; that needs approval from a code owner.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by looking at the relevant files and the advisory.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_0191gmHXnP84Aeq3re3d5txr", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Xivee17JNDwh2wp5V98Mgi", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_017RMb79gzDgPMURxcDmVEgN", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212", "confidence": 0.7}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The fix is simple: the docstring says ROUND_HALF_EVEN, but the code uses ROUND_HALF_UP. Under half-even, 2.675 \u2192 2.68 and 2.665 \u2192 2.66, which is what the tests expect. Creating the branch now.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01LkYkwq6daKjE2oTCM66acY", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-bankers-rounding", "from_ref": "main", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01JsAggV8bnxZzhQcQ6SuRiM", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-bankers-rounding", "message": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}], "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Wyx6oDcRCxNEvfPPid37XN", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/money-bankers-rounding", "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-money-bankers-rounding-08d3cd5986", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01CxJzt6F2ZurZ62LfUo6GFi", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001", "max_wait_s": 900, "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "CI passed. Opening the PR.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01LCtE2bJ6hR2r2Z7HCRNfiZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-bankers-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "## Summary\n`src/money.py::round_money` was documented as using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212) but actually used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, causing `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` to fail in the nightly build (e.g. `2.665` rounded to `2.67` instead of `2.66`).\n\n## Change\n- Switch `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\n## Testing\n- CI run `ci-0001` on `08d3cd5986`: passed.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-bankers-rounding", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The request timed out, so the PR may have been created anyway. I'll check before trying again.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_016Tu4L5CwbSpZBhqt3GHebz", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"state": "open", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "list_prs", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "PR #101 was created, but the reviewer request didn't go through. Adding alex now.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01C6y7tFy4u4XEJ1b5HoCm1N", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"number": 101, "reviewers": ["alex"], "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "request_review", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **The bug:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` said it used banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) but actually used ROUND_HALF_UP. So `2.665` came out as `2.67` instead of the expected `2.66`.\n- **The fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-bankers-rounding`, I changed the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` on commit `08d3cd5986` passed.\n- **The PR:** The request to open it timed out, so I checked the open PRs before retrying. The PR had been created, but with no reviewers, so I added alex separately rather than opening a duplicate.\n\nI couldn't confirm the FIN-212 requirement itself because the advisory lookup returned \"unknown advisory.\" I went by the docstring and the test. I haven't merged the PR; that needs approval from a code owner.", "type": "text"}]}]}